>>SOURCE FORMAT FREE
*> polymorphism, gcobol variant (COBOL side study, GCC 15 front end). Same program as polymorphism.cob: N=10000
*> objects of K=6 types in megamorphic LCG order, accumulator threaded through every object over M passes.
*> Dispatch: each type's apply subprogram is resolved ONCE into a FUNCTION-POINTER table (SET PP(k) TO ENTRY
*> "APPLYn", the vtable analogue) and the fold loop issues CALL PP(k) per object, so the N*M dispatches are
*> indirect calls through a table, not name lookups. (The first draft used CALL identifier, which makes
*> libgcobol call dlsym per dispatch: 76 percent of the instructions were libc symbol lookup.) Written for
*> gcobol's inline-arithmetic rules: BINARY-LONG / BINARY-DOUBLE items only, every operand of a hot
*> ADD/MULTIPLY/DIVIDE/MOVE/IF is a variable (named constants K-xxx), no COMPUTE/FUNCTION in the hot loop;
*> each APPLYn does MULTIPLY / ADD / DIVIDE ... REMAINDER.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. polymorphism-gc.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-M            BINARY-LONG VALUE 50.
01 WS-ARG          PIC X(16)         VALUE SPACES.
01 WS-N            BINARY-LONG VALUE 10000.
01 K-ONE           BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
01 K-SIX           BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 6.
01 K-65536         BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 65536.
01 K-1000          BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 1000.
01 K-LCG-A         BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 1103515245.
01 K-LCG-C         BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 12345.
01 K-LCG-M         BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 2147483648.
01 WS-S            BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 42.
01 WS-T            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-Q            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-TT           BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-TD           PIC 9.
01 WS-I            BINARY-LONG.
01 WS-PASS         BINARY-LONG.
01 WS-ACC          BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 1.
*> per-object store, in LCG generation order (megamorphic), 1-indexed
01 OBJ-T.
   05 OBJ-ENTRY    OCCURS 10000 TIMES.
      10 OBJ-TYPE  BINARY-LONG.
      10 OBJ-A     BINARY-DOUBLE.
      10 OBJ-B     BINARY-DOUBLE.
      10 OBJ-C     BINARY-DOUBLE.
*> the per-object program name the dynamic CALL resolves at runtime
01 WS-K            BINARY-LONG.
01 WS-KT           BINARY-LONG.
01 PP-T.
   05 PP           FUNCTION-POINTER OCCURS 6 TIMES.
01 WS-X            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-A            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-B            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-C            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 ED-ACC          PIC -(18)9.
01 ED-M            PIC -(9)9.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    ACCEPT WS-ARG FROM COMMAND-LINE
    IF WS-ARG NOT = SPACES
       COMPUTE WS-M = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-ARG)
    END-IF

    *> build N objects: type from the LCG HIGH bits, fields a,b,c = next LCG values mod 1000
    PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM K-ONE BY K-ONE UNTIL WS-I > WS-N
       PERFORM LCG-STEP
       DIVIDE WS-S BY K-65536 GIVING WS-TT
       DIVIDE WS-TT BY K-SIX GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER WS-T
       MOVE WS-T TO WS-TD
       MOVE WS-T TO OBJ-TYPE(WS-I)
       PERFORM LCG-STEP
       DIVIDE WS-S BY K-1000 GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER OBJ-A(WS-I)
       PERFORM LCG-STEP
       DIVIDE WS-S BY K-1000 GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER OBJ-B(WS-I)
       PERFORM LCG-STEP
       DIVIDE WS-S BY K-1000 GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER OBJ-C(WS-I)
    END-PERFORM

    SET PP(1) TO ENTRY "APPLY0"
    SET PP(2) TO ENTRY "APPLY1"
    SET PP(3) TO ENTRY "APPLY2"
    SET PP(4) TO ENTRY "APPLY3"
    SET PP(5) TO ENTRY "APPLY4"
    SET PP(6) TO ENTRY "APPLY5"

    *> fold acc through every object, M passes; DYNAMIC dispatch per object via CALL WS-OBJ-NAME
    MOVE K-ONE TO WS-ACC
    PERFORM VARYING WS-PASS FROM K-ONE BY K-ONE UNTIL WS-PASS > WS-M
       PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM K-ONE BY K-ONE UNTIL WS-I > WS-N
          ADD OBJ-TYPE(WS-I) K-ONE GIVING WS-K
          MOVE WS-ACC         TO WS-X
          MOVE OBJ-A(WS-I)    TO WS-A
          MOVE OBJ-B(WS-I)    TO WS-B
          MOVE OBJ-C(WS-I)    TO WS-C
          CALL PP(WS-K) USING WS-X WS-A WS-B WS-C
          MOVE WS-X TO WS-ACC
       END-PERFORM
    END-PERFORM

    MOVE WS-ACC TO ED-ACC
    MOVE WS-M   TO ED-M
    DISPLAY FUNCTION TRIM(ED-ACC)
    DISPLAY "polymorphism(" FUNCTION TRIM(ED-M) ")"
    STOP RUN.

*> LCG: s = (s * 1103515245 + 12345) & 0x7fffffff
LCG-STEP.
    MULTIPLY WS-S BY K-LCG-A GIVING WS-T
    ADD K-LCG-C TO WS-T
    DIVIDE WS-T BY K-LCG-M GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER WS-S.
END PROGRAM polymorphism-gc.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. APPLY0.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 K-MUL           BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 1000003.
01 K-P             BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 1000000007.
01 WS-T            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-U            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 WS-Q            BINARY-DOUBLE.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01 LK-X            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 LK-A            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 LK-B            BINARY-DOUBLE.
01 LK-C            BINARY-DOUBLE.
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LK-X LK-A LK-B LK-C.
    MULTIPLY LK-X BY K-MUL GIVING WS-T
    ADD LK-A TO WS-T
    DIVIDE WS-T BY K-P GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER LK-X
    EXIT PROGRAM.
END PROGRAM APPLY0.

